Count Pairs with Sum
You are given an array arr[] and an integer target. You have to count all pairs in the array such that their sum is equal to the given target.

Explanation:
For each element, calculate needed = target - arr[i].
The HashMap stores how many times each previous element has appeared, 
so if needed exists, add its frequency to count — each previous occurrence forms a valid pair.

count += map.getOrDefault(needed, 0);
map.put(arr[i], map.getOrDefault(arr[i], 0) + 1);

The important part: we count every previous occurrence of needed, not just whether it exists.

Code:
class Solution {
    int countPairs(int arr[], int target) {
        // code here
        int count=0;
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            int needed = target-arr[i];
            if(map.containsKey(needed)){
                count+=map.get(needed);
            }
            map.put(arr[i],map.getOrDefault(arr[i], 0) + 1);
        }
        return count;
    }
}
